# UI verification

After changing routes, components, or global styles, verify with Playwright before any other browser. Do not ask the user to click unless you are blocked. Do not open Chrome DevTools, and do not use the Cursor built-in browser, until the Playwright run for this change is done.

`pnpm test:e2e` is the pass/fail check. A screenshot is not a pass.

## Playwright first

1. Convex is up. `pnpm dev` starts Vite on http://localhost:3213 and `convex dev` when that server is not already running.
2. `pnpm test:e2e`. This wipes the dev deployment, then runs the suite. Run `pnpm seed` afterward only when a later check needs dishes.

The command reuses `pnpm dev` on http://localhost:3213 when that server is already running. Otherwise it starts one. The smoke spec is `e2e/app-smoke.spec.ts`. It opens the week plan, past plans (and one archived plan when a link is there), the recipe library, the shopping list, and history.

When the smoke does not exercise the change, add or extend a Playwright spec for that flow and run it. That spec is the verification. Keep edge cases that are not a user journey in Vitest.

The stop hook allows you to finish only when `pnpm test:e2e` passed for the current UI diff. Passing, then editing a UI file, means you run it again.

## Layout and motion

Playwright still runs first. Assert what a user would check: the control is visible, the text is present, the count is right, the panel is in view.

Use the `user-chrome-devtools` tools only after that, and only for a visual judgment a Playwright assertion cannot make: spacing, overflow, or motion.

1. Open the affected route.
2. Read console messages and fix errors.
3. Check the one visual fact the spec could not assert: spacing, overflow, or whether the motion ran.
4. Save a screenshot under `.cursor/verification/<yyyy-mm-dd>-<slug>/` when that judgment is visual.

## Git

Do not `git add` or commit `test-results/`, `playwright-report/`, or `.cursor/verification/`.

## Completion report

State that `pnpm test:e2e` passed, and name any spec you added. Give a screenshot path only when Chrome was needed for spacing, overflow, or motion. If the server or Convex will not start, say what blocked you.
